@node Pascal Lexical Elements
@section Lexical Elements

@subsection Keywords

Pascal reserves the following keywords (case-insensitive):

@table @code
@item and, or, not, in, div, mod
Logical and arithmetic operators
@item array
Array type declaration
@item begin, end
Block delimiters
@item case, of
Case statement
@item const
Constant declaration
@item do
Loop body delimiter
@item downto
Reverse range
@item else, then
Conditional operators
@item file
File type
@item for, to, while, repeat, until
Loop constructs
@item function
Function definition
@item goto
Unconditional jump
@item if
Conditional
@item label
Label declaration
@item nil
Null pointer
@item packed
Memory optimization
@item procedure
Procedure definition
@item program
Program identifier
@item record
Record structure definition
@item set
Set type
@item type
Type declaration
@item uses
Module inclusion
@item var
Variable declaration
@item with
Context binding
@end table

@subsection Identifiers

Identifiers follow standard rules:

@itemize
@item Case-insensitive
@item Start with letter or underscore
@item Contain letters, digits, underscores
@item Examples: @code{PlayerHealth}, @code{score}, @code{_temp}
@end itemize

